<DocsLayout title="Scripting Overview" description="What RelayCore scripting can do and when to use it">
  <h1>Scripting Overview</h1>

  <p>RelayCore's script engine runs on Deno/V8 with TypeScript hooks. It complements the <a href="/en/docs/rule-engine">rule engine</a>: rules excel at declarative matching and fixed actions; scripts fit branching logic, cross-request state, and dynamic computation.</p>

  <h2>Scripts vs rules</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Need</th><th>Use</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Rewrite headers or mock a fixed response by URL/method</td><td>Rules</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Transform bodies dynamically, aggregate stats, cross-request cache</td><td>Scripts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Manual breakpoints with UI-driven resume</td><td>Rules + Tauri / HTTP API</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Business logic (signing, token refresh, A/B routing)</td><td>Scripts</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Lifecycle hooks</h2>

  <p>Register callbacks on <code>globalThis</code> to run at each proxy stage:</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Hook</th><th>When it runs</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>onConnect</code> / <code>onDisconnect</code></td><td>TCP connect and teardown</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>onRequestHeaders</code> / <code>onResponseHeaders</code></td><td>HTTP headers (read/write)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>onRequest</code> / <code>onResponse</code></td><td>Full request/response including body</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>onWebSocketMessage</code></td><td>WebSocket frame interception</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>onError</code></td><td>Proxy or script errors with stage info</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>See <a href="/en/docs/scripting">Scripting API</a> for types and <a href="/en/docs/scripting-guide">Scripting Guide</a> for workflow.</p>

  <h2>Runtime features</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>TypeScript / npm</strong>: bundle with esbuild, load via CLI <code>--script</code> or HTTP <code>/api/v1/script</code></li>
    <li><strong>sharedState</strong>: cross-request in-memory state (per-isolate; good for counters and cache indexes)</li>
    <li><strong>relay.env</strong>: whitelist-controlled env access (<code>--script-env-allow</code>)</li>
    <li><strong>relay.fetch</strong>: optional sub-requests; disabled by default with allowlist and audit</li>
    <li><strong>relay.* helpers</strong>: uuid, hash, base64, json, and more</li>
    <li><strong>Rule context</strong>: <code>flow.matched_rules</code> and <code>flow.rule_variables</code> expose rule match results to scripts</li>
    <li><strong>Observability</strong>: script duration metrics via Prometheus (see <a href="/en/docs/observability">Monitoring</a>)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Minimal example</h2>

  <pre><code>globalThis.onRequestHeaders = (_ctx, flow) => &#123;
  flow.layer.data.request.headers.push(["X-RelayCore", "1"]);
  return flow;
&#125;;

globalThis.onResponse = (_ctx, flow) => &#123;
  if (flow.response?.status === 404) &#123;
    console.warn("404:", flow.id);
  &#125;
  return flow;
&#125;;</code></pre>

  <pre><code># Run with script hot-reload
relay-core-cli run --script ./hooks.ts --script-watch</code></pre>

  <h2>Compared to other script models</h2>

  <p>If you know Python addons (e.g. mitmproxy) or similar proxy extensions, the main differences are:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Language</strong>: TypeScript instead of Python; npm via bundle step</li>
    <li><strong>Headers</strong>: <code>[name, value][]</code> arrays preserve duplicate headers</li>
    <li><strong>Body</strong>: <code>body.content</code> is base64 — use <code>atob</code> / <code>btoa</code></li>
    <li><strong>Global state</strong>: <code>sharedState</code> instead of process-wide Python globals</li>
    <li><strong>Mock responses</strong>: prefer <a href="/en/docs/rule-engine">rule engine</a> Mock actions; scripts for dynamic logic</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Migrating from a Python addon</h3>

  <pre><code># mitmproxy
def request(flow):
    flow.request.headers["X-Custom"] = "value"

# RelayCore
globalThis.onRequestHeaders = (_ctx, flow) => &#123;
  flow.layer.data.request.headers.push(["X-Custom", "value"]);
  return flow;
&#125;;</code></pre>

  <h2>Same script, multiple hosts</h2>

  <p>One script can load consistently across shared runtime hosts:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><code>relay-core-cli run --script</code></li>
    <li>HTTP API <code>POST /api/v1/script</code></li>
    <li>Tauri <code>load_script</code> command</li>
  </ul>

  <p>CLI for local dev, HTTP API for web UI or automation, Tauri for embedded desktop apps. See <a href="/en/docs/architecture">Architecture</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
